    pr_ref:  # e60c
    description: "Source: a second outside reader (a fresh LLM session given only the help output and the cached files) reviewed a hypergumbo 9.2.0 self-run on 2026-11-13, cache f36c63310c791188/results/c872eb7a7e793eab/ac34c56c06ec1788, made after the fixes from the first review merged. Each claim was re-checked against those files and the code on dev fed15705d7, then measured on 20 repositories that are not hypergumbo (default sketch and --no-source, 8k/32k/128k). Scripts, the 120 sketches and results.txt: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/outside_reader_review2_11142026.\n\nOBSERVED, default sketch (with source), 20 repositories.\n1. Entry Points is byte-identical at 8k, 32k and 128k on 20 of 20. On the 14 with more than 57 entry points it shows exactly 57 at every budget: podman 57 of 500 (11%), sqlalchemy 57/450 (13%), killbill 57/362 (16%), lazygit 57/354 (16%), jedis 57/277 (21%), prometheus 57/247 (23%), kserve 57/189 (30%), nats-server 57/173 (33%), vite 57/155 (37%), mitmproxy 57/129 (44%), pydantic-core 57/91 (63%), pm2 57/69 (83%), caddy 57/67 (85%), alertmanager 57/63 (90%). The six with fewer (httpx, knex, mini-redis, poetry, ripgrep, express) show all of theirs.\n2. The same 14 with --no-source show 63-73 entries at 8k (alertmanager, caddy and pm2 show all of theirs: 63, 67, 69); at 32k ten of the 14 show 100% and the other four show killbill 82%, lazygit 84%, sqlalchemy 66%, podman 59%; at 128k all 14 show 100%. So the default sketch at 128k shows fewer entry points than --no-source at 8k.\n3. Data Models: six repositories have the section. With source it shows 78-83 models at 8k and stops at exactly 100 from 32k up on the four that have more: kserve 100/262 (38%), pydantic-core 100/290 (34%), sqlalchemy 100/193 (52%), mitmproxy 100/125 (80%). With --no-source all four show 100% at 32k.\n4. hypergumbo self-run: Entry Points holds 48.0 of 146.1 confidence mass (33%) at all three budgets and ends \"... and 30 more\", \"... and 67 more\", \"... and 22 more\" at 128k; Data Models holds 90.0 of 324.6 at 32k and 128k.\n5. What the budget buys instead. Source Files Content is 50-86% of the 128k sketch on all 20 (killbill and podman 50%, mini-redis 86%), most of it whole files: alertmanager 14 of 15 files whole, httpx 28 of 30, express 92 of 92; on the self-run ir.py (2,319 lines) and linkers/registry.py (1,436) are printed whole. Files excerpted at 32k are absent at 128k on jedis (4), vite (4), nats-server (3), sqlalchemy (1) and the self-run (cli.py, io_boundary.py); pm2 loses one from 8k to 32k.\n\nMECHANISM. sketch.py, with_source only: budget_for_eps = min(remaining // 3, 2000) and max_eps = budget_for_eps // tokens_per_symbol (35) = 57; budget_for_models = min(20% of remaining, 1500) and max_models = budget // 15 = 100. The caps are in ADR-0005 (\"With Source Mode\": Entry Points capped at 2000 tokens, Data Models at 1500), which gives the reason: \"The caps are generous enough that they only clip at large budgets (32k+) where the sections are already fully represented.\" Both halves are false on the measurement: the Entry Points cap binds at 8k on 14 of 20 repositories, and the clipped sections show 11-90% of what there is. The cap is also a count, not a size: 57 entries cost 2.9k-7.0k characters across the 20 (WI-subos-puhuv-busig-dalab-kivuz-vabav-sajuz-pomil notes the count-based sizing in passing). The mechanism behind item 5 (files dropped as the budget grows, whole files preferred to more excerpts) was not traced.\n\nASK. This is an ADR-0005 amendment, so the owner rules first. Candidates: (a) drop the fixed caps and let each section hold its percentage share, stopping when everything is shown; (b) keep a cap but make it a function of the budget; (c) cap a section only once it is fully shown, which is what the ADR says the caps do. Measure each on the 20 repositories before choosing (run_one.sh and analyze.py reproduce the tables). Acceptance, whichever is chosen: a larger budget never shows fewer entry points, data models or source files than a smaller one for the same repository; a section that says \"... and N more\" is at its stated share of the budget; the ADR's sentence about the caps matches what the code does on the measured set.\n\nGENERALITY (owner, 2026-11-13). The fix must be a rule that holds for any repository and any language. The hypergumbo self-run is only where the defect was first seen. A fix keyed to this repository's paths or file names, or one that works for one language only, does not close this item.\nThe caps are constants in the renderer, so every repository with more than 57 entry points or 100 data models has this, in any language (the 14 are Go, Java, Python, Rust, TypeScript and JavaScript)."  # e60c
